A||||4||jlruiz67||How important is Jet Coating ??||||5||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||02-04-2001||03:40 PM||||How importand is jet coating manifolds, does it extend the life of s.s. manifolds? Is it really worth the expence? Thanks for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||02-04-2001||04:03 PM||||My experience tells me not to do it again ...<P>I had HPC coat my stock exhaust manifolds on for my 88 GT with silver.  Within 300 miles, it was flaking off!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I am not having any problem with it on a cast iron manifold that I had polished or the pipes after the manifold flaking or doing any other weird thing.<P>I am NOT going to have any more done.  My opinion is ... not worth it.<P>Paul<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||8
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||02-04-2001||04:41 PM||||Must have not been a good coating , we had the headers done on our V8 corvair and our flat 6 , 3 years and there still in great condition. Did you try calling the coating place?? We had a problem with one intake manifold chipping and flaking , they took it back and re-did it for shipping costs.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||02-04-2001||05:26 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Must have not been a good coating , we had the headers done on our V8 corvair and our flat 6 , 3 years and there still in great condition. Did you try calling the coating place?? We had a problem with one intake manifold chipping and flaking , they took it back and re-did it for shipping costs.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I believe it is the stainless steel that the exhaust manifolds are made of and the high temperatures and rapid cooling that kills the coatings.  I have read about others with the Jet Hot coating having the same problem with <B>JUST</B> the exhaust manifolds.<P>Like I posted above ... I have had <B>NO</B> problems with the rest of the pipes or the cast iron manifold I had coated.<P>Plus, I sold the car (AND found the flaking when I was showing the engine off to the buyer!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>Paul<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||02-04-2001||05:46 PM||||If you want a clean rust and scale free look, you should try bbq black paint.  The stuff is really cheap in comparison to jet hot, and touch up is just a simple matter of spraying it on dare.||||reg||1
